cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use QEncode in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "QEncode Benchmark Suite"
authors:
  - given-names: Jovan
    family-names: Ilov
    affiliation: QEncode
abstract: >
  QEncode is an open-source benchmark standard and certification platform for
  reproducible VQE quantum chemistry evaluation. It provides fixed benchmark
  definitions (cc-pVDZ basis, chemistry-driven active spaces), a fully
  reproducible execution pipeline (PySCF → qubit Hamiltonian → Z2 tapering →
  VQE with UCCSD, hardware-efficient or ADAPT-VQE ansätze), Ed25519-signed
  certification artifacts, and a public leaderboard. Determinism is enforced
  rather than assumed: entries are generated single-threaded, against pinned
  dependencies, from a clean source tree, and each records its full environment.
  Suite v4.4 covers 16 molecules from H₂ to the H₁₀ chain (20 qubits before
  tapering), with 47 certified entries. Every entry also reports classical
  reference energies (HF, MP2, CCSD, CCSD(T)) and fault-tolerant resource
  estimates.
version: "4.5.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
url: "https://www.qencode-benchmark.org"
repository-code: "https://github.com/qencode-benchmark/qencode-benchmark"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum chemistry
  - benchmarking
  - variational quantum eigensolver
  - VQE
  - reproducibility
  - quantum algorithms
  - ADAPT-VQE
  - CASSCF
  - cc-pVDZ
  - DARPA QB-GSEE
  - leaderboard
